[{"result":{"data":{"json":{"id":"1526","stub":{"id":"1526","section":"5. Finn Rock to Leaburg Dam","altname":"","river":"McKenzie","difficulty":"IIstandoutIII","states":["USA-ORE"]},"primaryGaugeStatus":{"status":"medium-runnable","latestReading":{"value":"2650","dateTime":"2026-05-12T03:15:00.000Z","qualifier":"NORMAL"},"metric":"cfs","adjustedDifficulty":null},"pointOfInterests":[{"type":"put-in","description":"Finn Rock is a popular access point for a day trip on the McKenzie at one time owned by Rosboro Lumber Company before being purchased and signficantly improved by McKenzie River Trust following their acquisiton in 2015-16. The access works well for rafts. To reach this access head to Highway 126 mile 37.9 and turn onto Quartz Creek Road which takes you across the bridge to river left. A good ramp is available on the upstream river left side of the bridge. The site has a toilet, information kiosk, and parking area. Located at USGS river mile 54.","id":"5794","location":{"latitude":"44.12833","longitude":"-122.379668"},"name":"Finn Rock Boat Landing Put-in","distance":"0.05","photoID":"NqO5Z6GI1i6cvxPjsuauu","difficulty":null,"approximate":false},{"type":"rapid","description":"A fun little playspot early in the run. It is just upstream of the Nimrod Bridge. Located at USGS river mile 51.6.","id":"5801","location":{"latitude":"44.115605","longitude":"-122.420641"},"name":"Clover Point Playspot","distance":"2.53","difficulty":"II+","approximate":false,"photoID":"16498"},{"type":"access","description":"Informal access at Clover Park on river right below Clover Rapid. This access can be used as a take-out below Clover for those doing a short playboating session at Clover. The access requires finding the trail through the blackberries on river right upstream of the old Nimrod Bridge.","id":"O6fmDAQCEB2zF7tImxPgd","location":{"latitude":"44.113067","longitude":"-122.422128"},"name":"Clover Park Access","distance":"2.71","photoID":"tkig7J0e1yZS17p7jLKNP","difficulty":"N/A","approximate":false},{"type":"rapid","description":"A fun class II down the left side. Located at USGS river mile 51.","id":"5803","location":{"latitude":"44.10707","longitude":"-122.425152"},"name":"Eagle Rock Rapid","distance":"3.19","difficulty":"II","approximate":false,"photoID":"0"},{"type":"rapid","description":"Waves down the left through Nells. Located at USGS river mile 50.6.","id":"5805","location":{"latitude":"44.10833","longitude":"-122.43202"},"name":"Nells Rapids","distance":"3.55","difficulty":"II","approximate":false,"photoID":"0"},{"type":"access","description":"Silver Creek boat ramp is located at Highway 126 mile 33.9. Located at USGS river mile 49.9.","id":"5800","location":{"latitude":"44.11623","longitude":"-122.443076"},"name":"Silver Creek Boat Ramp","distance":"4.38","photoID":"16499","difficulty":null,"approximate":false},{"type":"access","description":"This access is at a Highway 126 mile 32.2. Located at USGS river mile 47.9.","id":"5799","location":{"latitude":"44.124356","longitude":"-122.468091"},"name":"Rennie Boat Ramp","distance":"6.37","photoID":"16500","difficulty":null,"approximate":false},{"type":"rapid","description":"Run the easy line to the right and avoid it or run the meat down the left. Located at USGS river mile 46.6.","id":"5804","location":{"latitude":"44.131798","longitude":"-122.489059"},"name":"Brown's Hole","distance":"7.62","difficulty":"II+","approximate":false,"photoID":"0"},{"type":"access","description":"This access can be used as a take-out if you don't want to run Marten Rapid which is the biggest rapid on this lower section of the McKenzie. It is located at Highway 126 mile 29.1. Located at USGS river mile 45.","id":"5795","location":{"latitude":"44.131623","longitude":"-122.51929"},"name":"Ben and Kay Dorris Boat Ramp","distance":"9.32","photoID":"16501","difficulty":null,"approximate":false},{"type":"rapid","description":"This is a great class III rapid that is the highlight of the run for those with skills to do so safely. An alternative take-out for those who don't want to run this drop is available just upstream at Ben and Kay Dorris State Park. Located at USGS river mile 44.8.","id":"5798","location":{"latitude":"44.129109","longitude":"-122.522794"},"name":"Marten Rapid","distance":"9.57","difficulty":"III+","approximate":false,"photoID":"16502"},{"type":"access","description":"This is a popular take-out for one of the better whitewater sections on the McKenzie and is just below Marten Rapid. It is reached by driving to Highway 126 mile 38.5 and then turning onto Thomson Ln. which heads down to the river. You can recognize it from the river by the suspension bridge across the river. Located at USGS river mile 44.1.","id":"5797","location":{"latitude":"44.127708","longitude":"-122.534953"},"name":"Prince Helfrich Landing","distance":"10.21","photoID":"40112","difficulty":null,"approximate":false},{"type":"access","description":"Access on river right where the river transitions to the reservoir at Leaburg Dam at Highway 126 mile 25.3. The access site is maintained by the Eugene Water and Electric Board as a condition of their hydropower license. It has a paved ramp, parking, and a toilet.","id":"LjhTlSDXpqlrKUqdV14b5","location":{"latitude":"44.145112","longitude":"-122.590013"},"name":"Good Pasture Access","distance":"13.92","photoID":"evvswbK7ieOAPMSic6HQ7","difficulty":"N/A","approximate":false},{"type":"takeout","description":"At Highway 126 mile 23.8 cross the river over Leaburg Dam. The last access before the dam is located on the upstream river left side of the dam. You can portage the dam and access the river immediately downstream of the dam on river left.","id":"5796","location":{"latitude":"44.138638","longitude":"-122.611209"},"name":"Leaburg Reservoir Boat Ramp","distance":"15","photoID":"q0OdEjRGkqatUujLgD7ls","difficulty":null,"approximate":false}],"alerts":[{"id":"101253187","title":null,"post_date":"2017-07-19 04:00:00+00","detail":"The Corps is reducing reservoir levels behind the dams to support maintenance and rehabilitation of the structures’ spillway gates. Cougar Reservoir drawdown begins July 15, 2017, as water managers gradually increase daily water releases up to 500 cubic feet per second (cfs). Another gradual increase begins Aug. 1, when water release will eventually reach 1,000 cfs. Normal water release for this time of year is about 580 cfs. Water managers will also begin gradually increasing daily water releases at Blue River Reservoir, reaching about 500 cfs by Aug. 1. Normal daily release from the dam is about 300 cfs.","user":{"name":"Thomas O'Keefe"}}],"photos":[{"id":"881348","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"883881","description":"","caption":"Leaburg Dam","poi_name":"","subject":"","author":"Thomas O'Keefe ©","poi_id":null,"photo_date":"2006-10-02T14:54:31.000Z","updated_at":"2025-04-14T14:54:32.000Z","url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/881348","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/881348"}},{"id":"16499","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"1763","description":"","caption":"Silver Creek Boat Landing","poi_name":"","subject":"","author":"Thomas O'Keefe &copy;","poi_id":"5800","photo_date":"2006-09-30T14:51:06.000Z","updated_at":"2025-04-14T14:51:09.000Z","url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/16499","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/16499"}},{"id":"16501","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"1763","description":"","caption":"Ben and Kay Dorris State Park Boat Ramp","poi_name":"","subject":"","author":"Thomas O'Keefe &copy;","poi_id":"5795","photo_date":"2006-09-30T14:51:06.000Z","updated_at":"2025-04-14T14:51:09.000Z","url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/16501","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/16501"}},{"id":"16498","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"1763","description":"","caption":"Clover Point","poi_name":"Clover Point","subject":"Steve","auth